Z||000005||pHoOl||03-16-2001||01:13 PM||||Alrighty, i guess i'm confused.  I've heard you guys talk about SVO mustangs before, but i don't think i knwo what they are.  i have heard of the SVT mustangs, aka mustang cobras.  Are these the same things?<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||03-16-2001||01:25 PM||||Nope. SVO Mustangs came out in the mid eighties (same vintage as Fieros) and had a turbo 4 cylinder that was much hotter then the turbo 4 that was available in early Mustang GTs. They are most easily spotted from the biplane rear wing on the hatch and if I'm not mistaken they have an NACA style intake offset to one side on the hood.<P>PS... Read all about it here--&gt; <A HREF="http://www.mustangsvo.org/svostory.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mustangsvo.org/svostory.htm</A> <p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 03-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||03-16-2001||01:55 PM||||The same Turbo 4 was even in the Thunderbird Turbo Coupe (correct me if I'm wrong). My cousin had one and we took it out to Vegas.<P>I wasn't impressed.<P>Some of the non GT Mustangs were pretty sad, I raced a friend of mine in an LX and BEAT him on a top speed run WITH AN 87 COUPE! I was the one who was lifting his hood to find out what was wrong! Seems that even with a V8 there was no way he could make power with such a dinky little TBI on the top of it.<P>I'll never forget the look on his face when I started pulling away from him in a four cylinder (with Hooker Tri Y header!)<P>I wasn't that impressed.<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 03-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||KRMFiero||03-16-2001||02:19 PM||||My friend Tony has a Chrysler New Yorker... We saw a Blue notchback on 295 (I was in passanger seat) we started racing, we one, the fiero lost  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  if that was anyone umm I hope there was something wrong with the fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000009||wjluciano||03-16-2001||03:26 PM||||I have ha 86 se converted from auto to 5 speed performance clutch and igniton ignition<BR>modified throttle boddies w/ custome headers.<BR>last night i ran a blue svo in riverside. w/ a passenger in my car now unless there was something wrong with that svo which i doubt because it was clean. he got smoked. that was my first race with my se I took right home and waxed her up.||||reg||10
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||03-16-2001||04:18 PM||||Merkurs also had the 2.3ltr Turbo motor. Ran 15psi boost box stock (10psi below 4000rpm, autos ran 10psi max) Great cars , a wee bit of lag though. Mine wouldn't beat my 4spd GT in the 1/4 (bot cars being stock) but on the highway the car would pull 145mph @ 18psi boost with an Inetcooler....<P>JM<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 03-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||terryk||03-16-2001||04:33 PM||||SVO's were 2.3L Turbo Intercooled 245HP beasts. Running correctly, the SVO is the clear winner.<P>I drove one a few times. It was slow off the line but once the boost came on, it was up that tree, into that ditch or across those six lanes of freeway.||||reg||1
Z||000012||BBBAD GT||03-16-2001||04:39 PM||||I have an 86 SVO I now drive on a daily basis (only 38k miles!).  From the factory, they were rated at 200 hp (175hp for 84-85 models), and run 15lb of intercooled boost (thats why the big scoop is on the hood, feed the air to air intercooler).  It is a fun car, but brut speed isn't the reason they made it, it was for open track action with its 4 wheel disc brakes (bigger in front than the std mustang), Koni shocks, and better weight distribution because of the 4 banger up front.  They only made them from 1984-1986, with about 3k produced a year.  At that time, it was the only Ford to have 16" wheels, rear discs on a mustang, and the highest boost of any car company at 15lb.  By today's standards, it not that great of stuff.<P>My honest opinion between my old stock 87 Fiero GT and this 86 SVO is that the Fiero naturally has more torque off the line and down low, but the SVO will come on like a run-a-way train above 2500 rpms as its building boost.  Hate to say it, but the SVO would just flat out kill my old Fiero.  <P>Just my opinions from somebody who has owned both.... <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">      <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT (sold)</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000013||AL||03-16-2001||06:34 PM||||well all i can say is that he was spinning and i was gone,he was catchin me,that if we had more road, he would of spanked me.on the second run he had the car reving high,that when they said go he popped out, but again spinning tires, at that point i had a 1/2 a car length lead but this time i did't make my trany shift into second gear that he came on me and that was it.but my fiero hung in there quite nicely,but i'm lookin for my 3.4 firebird engine to stick into my car.<BR><B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif"> <BR>86gt<BR>84indy<P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||terryk||03-16-2001||07:39 PM||||I thought the final year of the SVO had the HP as the 5.0L GT, but most sites show 200 or 205 HP for the last year and 240 ft lbs of torque. Maybe that's the number I remember. <P>Still, it was a fun car. All or nothing.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 03-16-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000015||BBBAD GT||03-16-2001||09:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>I thought the final year of the SVO had the HP as the 5.0L GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You are right, the 302 GT was only rated at 200 hp in 1986, and then in 1987 they stepped up to better heads/cam to get the 225 hp rating.  <P>AL:  Whenever you beat a car that obviously has more HP, you need to pat yourself on the back, because it was pure driver that won, not ultimate HP (this happens more so than people think, espically on the street).<P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||N_Man||03-16-2001||09:56 PM||||Slammed, you said your Merkur was stock right?<BR>Well if it was im having a REAL HARD TIME believing 145mph.<BR>Reason being is that i used to own a merkur 5 spd transmission, and i have had it redlined in 5th MANY times, pulled strong to redline but at redline i was at about 200kph about 125mph.  Now this is estimated because the guage cut off at 85mph but still had ticks no numbers, so i made a mental note of where the needle was and counted, about 125mph<BR>Now if they changed the tranny gears later in production please excuse this but i had to say it.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Slammed Fiero||03-16-2001||10:38 PM||||I didn't mean it to sound like it was stock when I ran 232Km/h (145) It had an adjustable boost control from Turbo city and a Junk yard intercooler. I actually swapped between 2 intercoolers a Volvo one and a Sabb one. The Sabb was the best , as I had it mounted in the front opening with no lisence plate. The volvo Unit sat atop the motor much like a WRX subaru , I had a mustang scoop on the car on a junk yard hood. i never really liked the looks of the Mustang hood scoop set up so I re engineered the setup. The 145 was recorded with the front mount IC , I wouldn't be suprised if the speedo was off , but I know my friends Mustang dropped off at 125mph , so it was between 135-145 mph. who knows how accurate the speedo was. Stock I could get it to maybe 210 or so. This was a very clean car , never saw a winter and had 60,000 miles on it. Synthetic oil always used , former owner was a preist actually. The Tires were stock sized , it had Rappido bars on it (although I don't think they were made by rappido) it was an 86 so it had the By plane wing. <P>The inside of the turbo housing was polished as well with a 3M polishing kit. Typically the tranny started to get a little iffy in 2nd gear , We got into other things and it sat. <P>Fun car, But I was raised on healthy Torque curves.... I cringed everytime I launched the car , knowing that the tranny is a rare unit , and I didn't want to swap to a T5 from a mustang<P>Well enough off topic rambling<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000018||AL||03-16-2001||11:08 PM||||you are right bbbad,cause on the first run i hit it, and this wasn't power shfting my automatic,it was all foot and knowing when to ease on it just enough so the tranny could shift just right,cause when i pulled it the first time,my motor hit high but i let go just enough so it could change gears and when it did i quicky hit passing gear and i was a full car ahead,on the second run i missed the gear change and it was to late.I think if i had a 5 speed i would of took him easily,this svo is a 84 but just the same my little baby can hold her own.after all was said and done he had a chip on his shoulder cause he barely beat me,so i said ok let's see you beat my trans am,he passed.<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif">  <BR>86gt <BR>84 indy 4 speed<P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||14
Z||000019||Phantom Rage||03-17-2001||05:02 AM||||Here are some stat's for an early SVO.  Pretty impressive for an 84, just incase anyone is interested.  Just be careful when racing one of these suckers.  1) Certain later model years came with more horsepower and torque.  2) They are easy to modify and a good majority of them are!!!  <P>As observed from: Road and Track Oct 1983 issue <P>Curb Weight = 3090<BR>BHP = 175HP<BR>Torque = 210Lb-Ft<BR>lb/bhp test weight = 18.6<BR>1/4mi = 15.8@89mph<BR>0-60mph = 7.7<BR>Lateral accel, 100 ft radius = .825<BR>700-ft slalom = 63.9<BR>60-0 = 158<BR>80-0 = 277<P>||||reg||7
